college|educational-institution|NOUN|institution for further or higher education|An educational institution offering further, higher, or specialist education.|trường cao đẳng; trường đại học; cơ sở đào tạo chuyên ngành|She chose a local college that offered evening design classes.|Cô chọn một trường cao đẳng địa phương có các lớp thiết kế buổi tối.|Countable as an institution; at college and go to college often omit the article. Its educational level varies by country.|0
extent|degree-or-range|NOUN|degree or range of something|The degree, size, or range of something.|mức độ; phạm vi|We did not know the full extent of the storm damage until daylight.|Chúng tôi chưa biết đầy đủ mức độ thiệt hại do bão cho tới khi trời sáng.|Usually singular in the extent of something; to some extent qualifies how far a statement is true.|0
maths|study-of-number-and-shape|NOUN|study of numbers, shapes, and patterns|The subject that studies numbers, shapes, quantities, and their relationships.|toán học; môn toán|Our maths lesson used paper folding to explore symmetry.|Tiết toán của chúng tôi dùng việc gấp giấy để tìm hiểu tính đối xứng.|British short form of mathematics; takes singular agreement, as in maths is useful. American English commonly uses math.|0
reassure|make-less-worried|VERB|make someone feel less worried|To say or do something that makes someone feel less worried or uncertain.|trấn an; làm yên tâm|The guide reassured us that there was enough time to catch the ferry.|Hướng dẫn viên trấn an chúng tôi rằng vẫn còn đủ thời gian để kịp chuyến phà.|Transitive reassure someone; reassure someone that a clause or about something explains the concern.|0
terrible|very-bad|ADJECTIVE|very bad or unpleasant|Very bad, unpleasant, or upsetting.|rất tệ; kinh khủng; rất khó chịu|The broken microphone made a terrible noise during rehearsal.|Chiếc micro bị hỏng phát ra tiếng động rất khó chịu trong buổi tập.|Used before nouns or after linking verbs; terrible at an activity describes very poor ability. The evaluation depends on context.|0
